[[Hans Wegner]], Denmark, 1949. Also called the CH24.

A wood frame and a seat woven from paper cord. Nothing else.

[[Truth to Materials]] in natural materials. The whole chair could go back to the soil.

What is it arguing? Was this intended as a [[Bioregional|BioRegion]] chair at its creation? or were they just making chairs the way you made chairs at the time?

Did Wegner or [[Carl Hansen & Son]] think ideologically about this chair? or was it really just meant to be a simple, beautiful object for sitting

It is an object that has extreme [[Chair-ness]] for me.

See [[We used to know how]], [[By intent or by habit?]]
